	<title height="200">
		<element kind="staticText" uuid="0178a073-c78d-5066-a7d1-43ac4dba7c90" x="0" y="10" width="515" height="30" fontSize="22.0" hTextAlign="Center">
			<text><![CDATA[Okapi Barcode Sample]]></text>
		</element>
		<element kind="textField" uuid="bf71a079-0e3e-50f8-b7b2-bac7495ca6f6" x="0" y="50" width="515" height="20" fontSize="12.0" hTextAlign="Center">
			<expression><![CDATA["This sample uses Okapi Barcode Version 0.5.7"]]></expression>
		</element>
		<element kind="textField" uuid="132e3190-fa49-578d-874d-d274668c23ac" x="0" y="70" width="515" height="20" fontSize="12.0" linkType="Reference" hTextAlign="Center">
			<expression><![CDATA["https://github.com/woo-j/OkapiBarcode"]]></expression>
			<hyperlinkReferenceExpression><![CDATA["https://github.com/woo-j/OkapiBarcode"]]></hyperlinkReferenceExpression>
		</element>
		<element kind="staticText" uuid="c715f3a4-24ba-5173-9c37-114fe33aba34" x="0" y="100" width="515" height="95" style="Type Note">
			<text><![CDATA[Each barcode type has its own okapi:* component. The types are arranged in sections: general-purpose linear barcodes, retail and GS1 barcodes, industry-specific linear barcodes, stacked barcodes, 2D barcodes and postal barcodes. Each type is shown first with the default settings, then with each setting it supports. The settings every type has are combined in a few more barcodes: the human-readable text, the quiet zones with colours, alignment and rotation. The caption above each barcode lists the settings that differ from the defaults, and the code when it differs from the one given for the type. The thin grey frame is the element's border: it shows how the barcode is sized and aligned in the element. moduleWidth, quiet zones and bar heights are in report units. The alignment examples set a moduleWidth that leaves free space in the element; barcodes with a fixed shape are aligned in the space they leave. "Rotated Right" is a style with rotation="Right": the components take their rotation and alignment from the element style when they don't set them.]]></text>
		</element>
	</title>
</jasperReport>
